# architecture-evaluation

Apply the architecture-evaluation skill when the request matches its scope.

Capabilities:
- frame stakeholders, concerns, viewpoints, views, and rationale using ISO/IEC/IEEE 42010 concepts
- convert architecture-significant requirements into measurable quality attribute scenarios
- compare alternatives with explicit trade-offs, sensitivity points, risks/non-risks, and reversibility
- produce and validate an ArchitectureArtifact with ADR and fitness-function handoffs

Stop when: The fixed-point context, stakeholders and concerns, quality scenarios, alternatives, trade-offs, sensitivity points, risks/non-risks, reversibility, operational concerns, approvals, and downstream handoffs are explicit; the ArchitectureArtifact validates or is marked blocked with schema errors.
